From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] widl: only an interface can have [async] procedures (5911)

fast-a 3309's is_async_rpc_func asked is_object() about every interface type
a function is written for, including a dispinterface, and is_object asserts
on that: widl aborted on dlls/oleaut32/tests/tmarshal.idl, so a build with the
conformance tests failed (the release build, with --disable-tests, did not
reach it). [async] is checked first and only an interface is asked.

Integration patch (integ-2026-10). Found by the integration's tests build.
Gates: widl-pipe, rpcrt4-async-rpc, rpcrt4-pipe (3309-3311).
---
diff --git a/tools/widl/typegen.c b/tools/widl/typegen.c
--- a/tools/widl/typegen.c
+++ b/tools/widl/typegen.c
@@ -1376,7 +1376,8 @@ static unsigned int write_old_procformatstring_type(FILE *file, int indent, cons
  * RPC_ASYNC_STATE of the call, NAME_AsyncHandle, which the format strings don't describe */
 int is_async_rpc_func( const type_t *iface, const var_t *func )
 {
-    return !is_object( iface ) && is_attr( func->attrs, ATTR_ASYNC );
+    /* only an interface has attributes to tell (a dispinterface or module method is never one) */
+    return is_attr( func->attrs, ATTR_ASYNC ) && type_get_type( iface ) == TYPE_INTERFACE && !is_object( iface );
 }
 
 int is_interpreted_func( const type_t *iface, const var_t *func )
